WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.380
I've never heard of a cattle prod.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.540
There are stories of back
rooms without cameras

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.130
where guys get roughed up a little bit.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.780
Nowadays, we don't need to do that.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.520
Hello, everybody. My name's Brian Stanton.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.340
I'm a casino executive in Las
Vegas for Station Casinos.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.100
I have 20 years in the
table-games business

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.500
watching and looking at game security.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.579
Today, we're going to be looking at

00:00:23.579 --> 00:00:27.577
casino-heist movie scenes
and judge how real they are.

00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:32.040
Whoo! You are a winner!

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.040
Inside jobs, collusion is
a thing that we worry about

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.798
and a thing that we look into.

00:00:36.798 --> 00:00:39.490
There's been numerous stories of dealers

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.023
setting up bets that aren't there

00:00:41.023 --> 00:00:42.750
or paying bets that aren't there,

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.520
because they're in
collusion with a player.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.110
Things they're doing stand out.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.910
So, when I'm walking the floor,

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.890
if I see dealers turning their head

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.320
and looking where I'm at or
where their supervisor's at,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.270
they want to know where we're at

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.545
because something's going on.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.020
Security measures.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.113
When the system senses a threat,
it shuts down and reboots.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.170
Well, for how long?

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.030
Man: Three minutes and 20 seconds.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.860
I've been in a few older properties

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.410
where something will happen
with a power transformer.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.970
Power goes out in the city.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.100
If we lose surveillance
coverage, we stop playing.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.560
If we have no camera
coverage to the games,

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.530
we just pull the lids up, lock
the games, and wait it out.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.240
We wouldn't deal the games

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.430
or operate without surveillance coverage.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.870
The system's in lockdown.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.810
All calls in and out of
this room are secure.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.360
Again, sir, it's in lockdown.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.190
It's a very Hollywood scene

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:36.330
that is completely unrealistic
for a multitude of reasons.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.230
First of all, their surveillance room

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.703
looks like an NSA SCIF.

00:01:39.703 --> 00:01:41.520
It's the nicest room I've ever seen,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.250
and no surveillance room
I've been in is that nice.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.040
They're not controlled by computers,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.150
where you could be locked out

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.560
and couldn't make a phone call.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.570
I don't think there's a scenario

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.550
where we would be stuck in a room.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.770
I would hope that there's
some government agency

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.210
like OSHA who would protect us

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.650
from being locked in a room.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.730
As a business practice,

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.580
we would have a hard-line
phone in every office,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.340
and surveillance would
always be able to use that.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.890
Obviously, if power went
out, that may go out with it,

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.380
and then we'd have to
use the old-fashioned

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.605
find the person and tell
them what's going on.

00:02:15.092 --> 00:02:15.925
Whoa!

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.340
Bringing in dice has happened.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.140
I haven't seen it in my career,

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.290
but I've heard stories in that
time frame of it happening.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.400
And they wouldn't be magnetic.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.950
They would be loaded, where
you would add some weight

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.120
to one side or another,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.040
or you would shave some corners.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.903
This is very Hollywood. The whole lighter

00:02:33.903 --> 00:02:36.570
and seeing it flip so slowly

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.950
from one side to another.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.828
I would hope my supervisors
would catch that

00:02:39.828 --> 00:02:41.310
right away if it was possible.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.020
And they wouldn't get away
with a whole lot of money,

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.561
because it's pretty obvious.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.680
Getting that amount of
bets for the numbers

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.870
that they kind of had
over everybody's heads,

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.900
apparently there's no table
maximum on any of these games,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.030
which is unrealistic as well.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.790
I think I saw a $100,000
bet on a snake eyes,

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.700
which, I think $500's
about the most I've seen

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.960
as a limit for that.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.750
Every bet on every table
has a maximum-amount bet.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.990
All very, very unlikely and comical.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.982
For accuracy of casinos,
I rate it about a 2.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.300
I would love to know if
a mathematician out there

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.310
ever looked at any of
those equations on there

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.900
and figured out if it was anything.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.100
Card counting is not some
extravagant trigonometry problem.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.750
It's just basic counting.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.640
Second of all, you really can't learn

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.100
card counting in one day, reading a book.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.465
The general public knowing about it

00:03:39.465 --> 00:03:40.800
has probably been a boon for us,

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.510
because people think they
can come out and do it,

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:43.585
and they really can't.

00:03:48.135 --> 00:03:49.620
[screaming]

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.536
If you're going to count
cards, you probably wouldn't

00:03:51.536 --> 00:03:53.585
attract that much attention to yourself.

00:03:53.585 --> 00:03:55.348
You have the character in the background

00:03:55.348 --> 00:03:57.373
flipping off the cameras,

00:03:57.373 --> 00:03:59.431
creating a lot of energy around

00:03:59.431 --> 00:04:00.988
and drawing attention to themselves.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.030
Splitting fives.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.980
Noticing that they're doing things, again.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.470
He did split fives,
which you would never do,

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.120
even if you were a card counter.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.620
You would have to maybe
know what the next three

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.060
or four cards coming out of the shoe were

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.320
to make that make sense.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.325
He can't lose! He can't lose!

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.940
The floor supervisor and the pit boss

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:21.900
talking to each other.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.090
We wouldn't need to cover
our mouths with a clipboard.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.380
They're not going to read our lips.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.720
It would be, "Hey, something's
going on over there.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.340
We're watching it on camera.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.740
Let's make a plan for what
we're going to do about it."

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:36.390
[screaming]

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.730
Doing a distraction to escape
doesn't make any sense,

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.500
'cause they still have
to cash the chips out.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.880
Counting cards is not illegal,

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.190
unless you're using some device

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.660
to give yourself an advantage.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.660
Smartwatch or a computer in
your shoe or on your thigh,

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.580
that would make it cheating a game.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.170
But keeping track in your head

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:55.410
and knowing how many big
cards versus little cards are,

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.650
you can gain an advantage,
and so it's frowned upon.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.110
If somebody's card-counting
in a Las Vegas casino,

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.670
we simply say, "Hey, you're not welcome

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:03.900
to play blackjack anymore.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.430
Your action's too good for us."

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.550
This scene, not very
realistic in that regard.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.120
1 for accuracy of how
we do things in a casino

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.568
or representing how
card counters would act.

00:05:14.568 --> 00:05:18.120
Ace: Cash flows from
the tables to our boxes,

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.440
through the cage,

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:23.310
and into the most sacred room
in the casino, the count room.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.590
It's not realistic to a modern casino

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.020
as far as how you would
enter it, how it's laid out,

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.090
or how the actions are
actually taking place.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.490
You see the keep-out sign,
and then they walk in.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.342
We wouldn't allow anybody to walk in

00:05:34.342 --> 00:05:36.090
with a briefcase nowadays.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.770
The workers that walk in are walking in

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.630
with clear purses, if at all.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.480
The count room is the most
secure room in the building.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.180
There are procedures in
place for who can go in,

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.400
how they can go in, what they
can do when they're there.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.800
Probably in part because
these things did happen

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.140
when they were run by
individuals or by the mob,

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.720
versus now, publicly traded companies.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.880
Nicky: They're counting
money. Who wants to bother?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.400
And the best part was that
upstairs, the board of directors

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.740
didn't know what the f--- was going on.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.840
I mean, to them, everything
looked on the up and up.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.030
But when you're paying out at the cage,

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.050
we would count by hand.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.228
And they did a good job of
how their hand motions were

00:06:09.228 --> 00:06:10.530
and how they laid the bills out.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.710
Every table, there's a paddle
to the right of the dealer,

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.660
and they take the cash, and
they drop it into a slot,

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.370
and it goes into what's called a drop box.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.900
And those are collected daily,

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.490
and they're double-lock-secured.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:22.830
And security would come
around and remove them,

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.300
take them into the count room,

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.733
where it's unlocked and the money is just

00:06:25.733 --> 00:06:27.300
dropped out onto a clear table.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.500
And then the money is counted

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.660
and sorted and assigned to that table.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.670
Nicky: The guys inside the counting room

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:36.480
were all slipped in there
to skim the joint dry.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.240
They'd do short counts,
they'd lose fill slips,

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:41.730
they'd even take cash right
out of the drop boxes.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.920
It's in a time period, back in the day,

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.080
where you hear stories
about these things going on.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.600
A fill slip is just an order form

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.850
when a table game needs more chips.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.040
Throughout the day, as
people get up and walk away

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.140
and cash out, we have to
replenish those chips.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.120
And you order a fill from the cage

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.680
to bring more chips to the table.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.880
And that's how you figure out

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.490
how much a table wins
or loses in a given day.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.170
Nicky: And it was up to
this guy, right here,

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.600
standing in front of about $2 million,

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.100
to skim the cash off the top

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:11.640
without anybody getting
wise, the IRS or anybody.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.560
The skim was apparently a real thing

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.570
that the mob was doing to the casinos.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:18.420
Casinos are big business, so
it takes a lot of employees

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.600
to factor in the cash that comes through

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.910
and the accounting paperwork
that goes along with that.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.230
So it is a very busy room,

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.850
there's a lot of people working,

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.680
but not busy enough
that we wouldn't notice

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.210
somebody walking in with a briefcase

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.560
and walking out with the cash.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.660
It takes key access,

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.390
and there's also cameras
everywhere nowadays.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.620
Ace: You can spot these a--holes

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.600
by watching the way they bet.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.770
Like this guy.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.780
He's betting lavender chips at $500 each

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.430
with only one little problem.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.720
He's always guessed right.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:48.090
When things stand out, you
take a closer look at it.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:51.060
So they did a great job of
how the dealers are moving,

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.890
how they're paying, how
they're putting cards

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:56.040
on the tables, to how the
supervisors stand in the pit,

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.020
to even how De Niro's character

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.570
walked in and started to observe things.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:02.010
Ace: I saw that the dealer was weak,

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:03.660
but he wasn't in on it.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.045
He just wasn't protecting his hand.

00:08:06.045 --> 00:08:08.280
He was lifting his hole card way too high.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.080
The first thing he noticed was

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.760
that the guy always guesses right.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.290
Kind of bends down to tie his shoe

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.270
so he can get a look at what's going on

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:16.920
and where those angles are coming from

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.530
and figures out that there's
a cheater on the other side.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.042
Ace: Signaling his buddy.

00:08:21.042 --> 00:08:24.270
They cruise from casino to
casino looking for weak dealers

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.520
the way lions look for weak antelope.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.460
Using a device to cheat, at
least in the state of Nevada,

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:32.310
is a crime, so you don't
see that nearly as often.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.690
Things like that used to happen

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:35.730
as computer technology took hold.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:37.050
If it wasn't for the device,

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:38.820
they wouldn't really be
doing anything wrong,

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.680
just taking advantage of a weak dealer.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.410
Those were the way we used
to check the hole card,

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.990
was for them to cover
it up and look for it.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.970
Nowadays we have a thing
called a peeker device,

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.178
which is a two-way mirror

00:08:49.178 --> 00:08:51.386
that they slide the cards right into

00:08:51.386 --> 00:08:54.232
so that there's no risk of
exposing that card anymore.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.430
Ace: Turns out this guy
and his f---ing pals,

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:04.890
they were knocking this
place dead for years.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.300
I've heard a lot of stories.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.830
I've never heard of a cattle prod.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.990
There are stories of back
rooms without cameras

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.580
where guys get roughed up a little bit.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.110
Nowadays, we don't need to do that.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.540
We have the Nevada Gaming Control Board,

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.680
we have security,

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:17.880
where we would just notify

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.740
and do everything through a legal process.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.110
It's once they brought
that device into play.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:23.550
And we'd notify the gaming commission,

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:25.590
say, "Hey, we have somebody
that we suspect of cheating."

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:26.970
And we would hand it right off to them.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.850
I think the movie was done incredibly well

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:31.590
from a technical standpoint.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.200
Everything outside of the cattle prod.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.788
That knocks the clip down to about a 7½.

00:09:36.788 --> 00:09:38.603
Charlene: Oh, my God, I can feel a kick!

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:42.960
Shelly: F---ing amateurs.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.580
This is a more realistic thing

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.080
that could happen and has happened.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.310
It's switching out dice.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.290
Fake dice, incredibly uncommon.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.930
Alec Baldwin's character
coming up as the casino boss,

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.700
somebody with the experience
to be able to see,

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.250
hey, the way he's cupping his
hand when he picks them up,

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.810
or the way he's releasing them

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:00.150
where fingers are bent up
to try and hide something.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:01.290
We have policies for that too.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.660
When a shooter shoots,
the supervisor's looking

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.610
for their hand to be open to make sure

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.050
they're not hiding dice in there.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:08.850
Cheating on dice can be common

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.560
because there's a lot going on.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.480
There's a lot of players,
there's a lot of distraction.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.490
The biggest cheating scam that happens

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.200
is what's called dice sliding,

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.960
where you would set one dice to a number,

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.550
and then when you go to throw them,

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.850
instead of the dice tumbling
and becoming a random result,

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.680
they can control one or both of the dice

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.000
and know what the outcome is

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.830
and either bet with it or against it.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:32.250
It takes a crew of people.
Someone to distract the dealer,

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.680
someone to throw it, another
one to make a big bet.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.780
So a couple times a year
you hear of a casino

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:39.030
getting hit with a dice-sliding team.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.250
Again, we have policies
and procedures in place

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.390
that protect us from that.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:44.190
They always have serial numbers on them.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:46.650
We make sure that they match
and that they're our dice.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.645
There is some security built into it.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:52.863
Yeah, he's up $18,000 since
I stepped up to the table.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.280
Sorry, Shelly. I'm kind
of hit or miss these days.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:59.580
In the scene, we see William
Macy acting as a cooler,

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.170
somebody who has such bad luck

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.460
that they put him at the table,

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:05.010
then his bad luck hopefully
rubs off on everybody else.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.900
Unfortunately, it is a thing.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.030
I haven't seen it in a long, long time.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:10.980
Managers throwing salt under a table

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.150
or pennies under a table,

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.370
because somehow that
was equated to bad luck.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:17.040
Modern casinos, I think, have
all gotten away from that

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.444
and just realized it's all about the math.

00:11:19.444 --> 00:11:21.777
Let's get it, let's get it!

00:11:21.777 --> 00:11:23.839
[everyone groaning]

00:11:25.347 --> 00:11:26.790
Aw.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:30.360
Guys, I thank you, my
pregnant wife thanks you.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:32.400
When he sensed that he
was going to get caught,

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.930
he said, all right, the gig's up,

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:35.910
and he switched back to the original dice

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.140
and happened to seven out.

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:39.630
Using your pregnant wife as a distraction,

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.390
this is a much more
realistic version of cheating

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:45.158
than the "Ocean's Eleven"
scene with the magnetic dice.

00:11:45.158 --> 00:11:47.340
Them switching out dice, I
think this is very accurate.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:48.490
I'd rate it an 8.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.640
I feel like you should
have somebody from the CIA

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.670
or FBI in here to evaluate
this, more than me,

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:02.880
because it doesn't pass
the smell test for me

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.680
on how casinos work

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.870
or anything that would happen in a casino.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.480
I think they say in the movie
it connects three casinos

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.460
that in reality are a mile apart.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.580
There's no secret bunker
anywhere with elevator in.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.200
And then the two security guards

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.480
just happen to be facing
away from the only elevator,

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:20.250
facing a door for no reason.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.260
Rusty: As your manager's
probably reporting to you now,

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.800
you have a little over $160
million in your vault tonight.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.998
You may notice we're only
packing up about half that.

00:12:28.998 --> 00:12:32.430
It would depend on how often
deposits are made to the bank

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.230
or whatever, but we are required

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.540
to be able to cover
any winners and losers.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.610
Now, does that mean we have
to give it to them in cash?

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.393
No. We just write them a check for it.

00:12:40.393 --> 00:12:42.480
Modern casinos, we've become

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.270
increasingly a cashless society,

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:48.353
and we have credit markers
and bank wire transfers.

00:12:53.422 --> 00:12:54.563
Yen?

00:12:54.563 --> 00:12:57.690
In previous clips, we saw
where the count room was.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.160
And then once the money's counted,

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.720
it's put into a secure location.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.550
You can call it a vault if you want to.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:06.960
But it being this far out
of the way, this protected,

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.120
like it's holding the nuclear codes.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.920
Benedict: Cue up the tape to the robbery.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:12.810
Installed on Tuesday.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.610
The images we saw of those
men robbing us was a tape.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.000
Walsh: What?

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.160
I feel safe to say that nobody has a vault

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.696
quite like this one, or
would we spend the money

00:13:22.696 --> 00:13:26.220
to inlay the marble, or
terrazzo, or whatever that was

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.050
with the name of the casino in the vault.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.940
That seems like we could spend that money

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:30.798
better somewhere else.

00:13:30.798 --> 00:13:32.880
I've worked at some
extravagant, opulent places,

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.022
but that's even a little bit over the top.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.780
Our directors of security,
our security managers

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:45.510
all either were former law
enforcement or know them,

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.430
so they would know when
these guys walked in.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.460
The likelihood of an
entire team of criminals

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:54.060
pretending to be Las Vegas
Metro or SWAT or whoever

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.320
and walking out with money,

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:56.850
I had a hard time watching this movie

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.230
when I watched it the first time.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.772
And I'm like, wow, I really have to

00:13:59.772 --> 00:14:01.873
suspend reality to enjoy this.

00:14:01.873 --> 00:14:05.280
A 1 on how things in a real casino look

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.780
or act or are run.

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:12.870
Cameras generally aren't at eye level

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.250
where you could spray-paint them.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:15.708
They're usually up in the ceiling.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:23.130
First thought is, that's probably the most

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:27.300
unsecure count room and
vault in any casino anywhere.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.040
Those look like regular office doors

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.470
and the locks that are on
my garage or back door,

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.480
as opposed to the locks that we would use.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:36.210
How the casino's laid out,
it's not very realistic.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:39.000
The count room is generally
pretty far back of house,

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.550
where it would take a couple of layers,

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:44.040
couple of access points
for someone to get to.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.690
There wouldn't necessarily need to be

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:48.600
a security guard in or
in front of that door.

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.167
There are security everywhere

00:14:50.167 --> 00:14:52.833
at the access points to
the back of the house

00:14:52.833 --> 00:14:55.692
that would take to get to that
hallway, to get to that door.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:58.595
I'm only going to say this once, OK?

00:14:58.595 --> 00:14:59.428
Who's listening?

00:14:59.428 --> 00:15:00.636
I am, yeah.

00:15:00.636 --> 00:15:02.310
What we would wear in the count room

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:05.610
is overalls with no pockets,
so that there was no ability

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:08.460
for anybody to hide
cash, chips, or anything.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:10.830
You would wear that uniform into the room

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:12.570
and not bring bags or anything with you,

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.755
so that you couldn't take
anything out of the room.

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:18.180
Main booth, scramble security.

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.920
Call Vegas PD. We need backup.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:22.620
While surveillance did notice
them after a few seconds

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:25.200
in the count room, they
would've noticed them

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:27.390
in the back of house, on
their way to the count room,

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:28.650
before that ever happened.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.030
Somebody's always watching.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.500
Obviously, once they did notice them,

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.400
they said notify metro, which
is exactly what we would do.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.880
Freeze! Hold it right there!

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.790
I would tell the security team,

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.290
and I think they would say the same,

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.230
we wouldn't engage on the casino
floor and risk a shoot-out.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.280
Not a wise idea.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.977
Let them get away with the
money, and we'll use our cameras,

00:15:49.977 --> 00:15:52.017
and we'll use metro, and
we'll track them down.

00:15:52.017 --> 00:15:55.440
We usually can see the getaway
car, see the license plate.

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.210
There has been some large thefts

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.100
throughout history of cages.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:02.820
And they are very usually
low-tech smash-and-grab hold-ups.

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:05.160
And I've yet to hear of
anybody getting away with it.

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:08.040
Armed robbery, that's more
realistic to what I've seen.

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:10.560
But overall, I'd say it rates about a 5.

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:14.068
Professionals always place
their bets through the croupier.

00:16:14.068 --> 00:16:16.200
Croupier: Two, six, 13.
Man: Two, six, 13.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.630
Croupier is a term we
don't use in the states.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:20.430
It's a European term for a dealer.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:22.980
He's obviously dealing
European or French roulette,

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:25.119
based on some of the bets that were made.

00:16:25.119 --> 00:16:26.536
No more bets, thank you.

00:16:29.723 --> 00:16:30.556
34 red.

00:16:30.556 --> 00:16:32.370
No, I'm sorry, sir, that's a late bet.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:35.070
How the player cheated is a normal move.

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.420
It's called past posting.

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:38.670
The dealer catches the past post,

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:39.960
but it's interesting how he caught it,

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.970
because he was staring
into the wheel head,

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:43.830
which is what we train them not to do.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.990
They should be watching the
layout for those past posts

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:48.780
and listening for the ball to
drop, and then glancing in.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:51.270
He would've had to have
memorized every bet on the table

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:53.010
to notice that that was a late bet.

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.570
Is there a problem?

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.940
Yes, this croupier's
accusing me of cheating!

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:58.250
I want to be paid!

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:01.650
Pay the gentleman. In full.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.678
When he does notice, the
supervisor comes over

00:17:03.678 --> 00:17:06.000
and gets involved and
asks what's going on.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.730
The gentleman acts aggressively.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:10.650
We probably wouldn't pay that bet.

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:13.170
We would use surveillance to
see that there was a late bet.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.060
Let's just get this guy
away from the table.

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:15.893
Let's go ahead and pay him

00:17:15.893 --> 00:17:17.490
knowing we still have to cash him out,

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:19.830
so we still have the ability
to recoup those funds.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.801
It's fairly realistic, from
the terminology they use

00:17:22.801 --> 00:17:25.380
to the motions of the dealer
to how the dealer's dressed.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:26.550
I rate this about an 8.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.280
My favorite casino-heist
movie is definitely "Casino."

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:30.720
I think, by far and away, "Casino"'s

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:32.234
the most realistic interpretation

00:17:32.234 --> 00:17:33.960
of what was done at that time

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.660
and how we've evolved to the modern time.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.943
